WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.922 --> 00:00:02.442
- Sofia.

00:00:02.442 --> 00:00:04.138
- [Sofia] Hi.
- Hi, I heard you have

00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:05.775
an imaginary friend.

00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:09.374
- I do, I do have one, I do
have an imaginary friend, yes.

00:00:09.374 --> 00:00:14.052
(quiet music)

00:00:14.052 --> 00:00:16.734
She was a deer named Erin.

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:20.577
And we had a plant in like a
house plant in our apartment

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:24.733
when I was a kid and I used
to dig up, like the roots

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:27.392
of this plant and
immediately blame it on Erin.

00:00:27.392 --> 00:00:29.272
And my parents like couldn't
do anything about it

00:00:29.272 --> 00:00:30.178
'cause they were like,

00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:32.998
"We have to let her have
her imaginary friend."

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:37.875
I think in my mind she was
like Bambi's mom or sister

00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:38.676
you know what I mean?

00:00:38.676 --> 00:00:41.671
I was like really upset when
Bambi's mom died as a kid.

00:00:41.671 --> 00:00:45.293
So I had like a connection to
like a female maternal deer.

00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:48.115
Definitely used her as a
scapegoat, like a hundred percent.

00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:48.892
- Hi.

00:00:48.892 --> 00:00:50.251
- You had an imaginary friend as a kid?

00:00:50.251 --> 00:00:51.318
- I did.
- [Interviewer] Or even

00:00:51.318 --> 00:00:52.654
til this day? (chuckles)

00:00:52.654 --> 00:00:53.536
- [Voiceover] Pete was a human.

00:00:53.536 --> 00:00:58.191
I was a very literal kid, so
Pete was basically like my,

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:01.036
sort of obnoxious little brother.

00:01:01.036 --> 00:01:04.123
I was the good kid and
Pete was the one who

00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:07.277
like set things on fire.

00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:08.810
Pete and I hung out a lot.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.654
I liked playing him in checkers,

00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:14.057
he was better at me in checkers.

00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:17.238
And I realized quickly
that when you play yourself

00:01:17.238 --> 00:01:21.424
in checkers the person who goes
second kind of always wins.

00:01:22.137 --> 00:01:23.298
- [Interviewer] Quanta.

00:01:23.298 --> 00:01:25.237
- Oh hey, what's up?
- [Interviewer] Hi.

00:01:25.237 --> 00:01:27.118
Do you wanna talk about
your imaginary friend?

00:01:27.118 --> 00:01:28.709
- Uh sure, yeah.

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:32.470
So I had like a few
imaginary friends growing up.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.320
One that was probably my
favorite was my friend Ralph.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:41.320
He had like a round face
and he had like curly hair

00:01:41.375 --> 00:01:42.973
and I think he was always wearing

00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:45.353
like a blue shirt for some reason.

00:01:45.353 --> 00:01:46.468
He was cool.

00:01:46.468 --> 00:01:49.694
We would play games together.

00:01:49.694 --> 00:01:51.704
We actually plotted one time,

00:01:51.704 --> 00:01:53.851
so I had like, I loved the Rugrats.

00:01:53.851 --> 00:01:56.788
Obviously everyone knew
that Angelica was evil.

00:01:56.788 --> 00:02:01.688
So we plotted to
(chuckles) kidnap Angelica.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.266
He made me do this.

00:02:03.266 --> 00:02:07.074
But we duct taped her hands together

00:02:07.074 --> 00:02:08.351
and duct taped her mouth.

00:02:08.351 --> 00:02:11.392
My mom told me I was like cursing at it,

00:02:11.392 --> 00:02:14.888
but it was Ralph that
was cursing at Angelica.

00:02:14.888 --> 00:02:17.906
He really was like,
kind of a violent person

00:02:17.906 --> 00:02:20.745
and kind of influenced me
to do crazy stuff like that.

00:02:20.745 --> 00:02:22.499
But he was, he was great.

00:02:22.499 --> 00:02:24.217
- Britney Ashley.

00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:25.622
This is your song.

00:02:25.622 --> 00:02:28.037
Um, I heard you had an imaginary friend.

00:02:28.037 --> 00:02:28.919
- [Britney Ashley] I had more than

00:02:28.919 --> 00:02:30.800
just one imaginary friend.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.679
I had a whole entire
imaginary baseball team.

00:02:33.679 --> 00:02:36.163
Every day after school when
I was in elementary school,

00:02:36.163 --> 00:02:40.063
I had a huge backyard and I would play,

00:02:40.063 --> 00:02:43.604
I would, you know curate
my own baseball practice

00:02:43.604 --> 00:02:45.695
to my whole invisible baseball team.

00:02:45.695 --> 00:02:47.680
They had names, it was generally,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.677
this is very sad, it was generally names,

00:02:49.677 --> 00:02:53.519
like kids names that I
wanted to name my children.

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:55.621
It was a lot unisex names.

00:02:55.621 --> 00:02:57.002
It was great.

00:02:57.002 --> 00:02:58.198
I'm insane now.

00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:01.553
- (chuckles) My imaginarys
friend's name was Dakota.

00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:03.956
Dakota was a bull.

00:03:03.956 --> 00:03:04.955
He was orange.

00:03:04.955 --> 00:03:07.938
Dakota was a little bit of
everything when I was growing up.

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:12.523
He was a cowboy obviously,
Samurai, a ninja,

00:03:12.523 --> 00:03:14.915
he was a paleontologist for a little bit.

00:03:14.915 --> 00:03:17.795
Yeah, but it wasn't like a bad influence.

00:03:17.795 --> 00:03:20.453
He was basically when
my friends couldn't play

00:03:20.453 --> 00:03:21.997
and I had to entertain myself.

00:03:21.997 --> 00:03:23.797
Me and Dakota went on adventures.

00:03:23.797 --> 00:03:26.014
He's probably a jet fighter now.

00:03:26.014 --> 00:03:27.941
'Cause that seems like
it would be really fun.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.379
But you put away childish things

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:32.039
and you become a boring adult.

00:03:32.039 --> 00:03:34.756
And Dakota is someone else's now.

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:39.568
(quiet music)

